  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Oxfam will promote human rights and environmental rights in areas affected by oil and gas projects mainly Tilenga Project and EACOPproject in Uganda. The interventions are aimed at upholding human rights and protecting EHRDs and hold government and Internationaloil companies accountable. we will support legal empowerment of EHRDs and exchange learning between selected defenders and project-affected persons from Tilenga, Kingfisher, and the East African Crude Oil Pipeline (EACOP) areas to share knowledge and experience. This exchange learning initiative will foster solidarity among project-affected persons (PAPs)/defenders and create a dynamic platform for the sharing of knowledge and encouragement among defenders and PAPs across these diverse areas. This will be through promoting working in networks and partnership and coalitions like Solidarity Network of Environmental Human Rights Defenders (SNEHRDs).

Oxfam will be supporting the ongoing legal cases (including the seven-community grassroots defenders case) and any other emerging legalissues directed to defenders and project affected persons (PAPs) in the Tilenga, EACOP and Kingfisher project areas in the districtof Hoima, Kikuube and Buliisa.  Oxfam will also conduct legal empowerment training (compliance and application of UN human rights mechanisms) for 40 participants who will act as ambassadors to others in order to enable EHRDs to carry on their work with informed minds of their rights and duties as citizens.
Strengthen established networks, partnerships and coalitions working on environmental and human rights issues in our communities to further the spirits of standing in solidarity with one another in times of needs amongst individual defenders and the local organizations.

Oxfam believes in reviving and strengthening networks and coalitions of local organizations/Individual defenders in Bunyoro like the Solidarity Network of Environmental Human Rights Defenders (SNEHRDs) will promote easy sharing of information concerning EHRDs&#x2019; security, resource mobilization, amplifying of one another&#x2019;s efforts to reach moreaudiences and have intended outcomes.
The grassroot EHRDs identify and build peer support groups to handle mental stress resulting from the work environment in each of the selected districts.</narrative>
  </description>
